{"availability":"available","full":"antonsoo/errorbars","name":"errorbars","description":"Error bars for LLM evals: clustered SEs, paired comparisons, leaderboards, and power analysis. Python + web calculator.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T09:53:22Z","updated":"2026-10-04T08:10:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://antonsoo.github.io/errorbars/","topics":["benchmarking","confidence-intervals","llm-evaluation","machine-learning","power-analysis","python","statistics","typescript"],"demo":"https://antonsoo.github.io/errorbars/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:02:42.625Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:02:42.625Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:02:42.625Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:11:24.297Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:42:36.410Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:02:42.625Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Error bars for LLM evals. Know whether model B is actually better, or you're reading noise.","LLM eval results get reported as bare accuracies — \"model B scored 71.2%, up from 69.7%\" — with no error bar, no significance test, and no accounting for the fact that the questions came in correlated groups. On a 500-question benchmark, a 1.5-point gain is very often noise: at a 50% baseline you'd need roughly a 9-point gap to reliably detect anything at 80% power, α=0.05 (errorbars power --n 500 --baseline 0.5 → minimum detectable effect ≈ 8.9 points). Evan Miller's \"Adding Error Bars to Evals: A Statistical Approach to Language Model Evaluations\" (arXiv:2411.00640, 2024) lays out the right…"],"features":["summarize — mean, SE, and 95% CI (CLT by default, Wilson for small-n binary scores,","bootstrap on request); clustered SE with design effect and ICC when a clusterid column is present; within/between-question variance decomposition when a sample column is present.","compare — paired mean difference, SE, CI, p-value; the correlation between the two models'","per-question scores and how much pairing shrank the SE vs. an unpaired comparison; a cluster-robust paired SE/p-value when clusters are present; exact McNemar test for binary scores.","leaderboard — every model with its CI, Holm-corrected pairwise paired tests, and groups of"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/errorbars/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"db29606a63ada8db0285e0a2c2e8816a5024d0a323ac7d16bc76c14c9b81decb","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:24.404Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:24.404Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Error bars for LLM evals. Know whether model B is actually better, or you're reading noise.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/errorbars/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"db29606a63ada8db0285e0a2c2e8816a5024d0a323ac7d16bc76c14c9b81decb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/errorbars/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:24.405Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T08:10:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/errorbars/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:24.406Z","hash":"db29606a63ada8db0285e0a2c2e8816a5024d0a323ac7d16bc76c14c9b81decb","originalBytes":17002,"storedBytes":17002,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["errorbars","model","one","questions","test","power","eval","inspect","tests","compare","every","leaderboard","run","logs","paired","exact","output","pairing","samples","bash","docs","examples","lm-eval","log","mean","out","reading","see","two","web","cluster","correlation","effect","error","question","sample","variance","when","against","clt","clustered","gap","how","json","mcnemar","p-value","per","summarize","accuracy","baseline","column","data","directory","fixtures","jsonl","metric","needed","only","planning","point","same","scores","several","statsmodels","table","tasks"